      <h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: #251F19;">Why this mattered for design</h3>
      <p style="margin: 0; max-width: 1080px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3B342D;">Understanding the API constraints early meant the interview-scheduling screens could be designed around what was actually feasible, e.g. showing real-time availability instead of promising a sync speed the calendar APIs couldn&#8217;t deliver, and designing a clear conflict-resolution state for when a double-booking occurred mid-sync.</p>
